---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const url = (path) => `${base}${path}`;
---
<BaseLayout title='Apos® Treatment — Miles Physio' description='Explore personalised Apos treatment with Miles Physio. Understand how it works, watch patient experiences, see pricing and book a free discovery call.' bodyClass='apos-page' styles={['/apos.css?v=1']} apos={true}>
<main id="main">
<section class="apos-hero section"><div class="apos-breadcrumb"><a href={url('/')}>Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Apos treatment</span></div><div class="apos-hero-grid"><div class="apos-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="mini-line"></span> Apos® treatment at Miles Physio</p><h1>A different approach<br>starts with<br><em>how you walk.</em></h1><p>When joint pain changes the way you move, everyday activities can start to feel harder.</p><p>Apos combines individually adjusted footwear with a personalised treatment programme, designed to help reduce pain and improve walking. At Miles Physio, we’ll help you understand whether it could be a suitable next step.</p><a class="button" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Book your free discovery call <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a><span class="micro">Talk through your symptoms. Ask questions. Explore your options.</span></div><div class="apos-hero-product"><img class="apos-brand" src={url('/assets/apos-logo.png')} alt="Apos" width="1324" height="447"><span class="hero-product-kicker">Personalised to your every step</span><img class="hero-shoe" src={url('/assets/apos-shoe.jpg')} alt="Apos footwear with two adjustable pods beneath the sole" width="2560" height="1707" fetchpriority="high"><div class="product-annotation"><span class="annotation-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Two adjustable pods.<br>A fit that’s individual to you.</span></div><div class="hero-product-footer"><span>Clinically guided</span><span>Built around you</span></div></div></div></section>
<nav class="page-nav" aria-label="On this page"><div><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#treatment">Your treatment</a><a href="#stories">Patient stories</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></div></nav>
<section id="overview" class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>01 / A closer look</span><span>Understanding Apos</span></div><div class="intro-grid"><h2 class="reveal">More than footwear.<br><span class="blue">A programme<br>built around you.</span></h2><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">Apos is a foot-worn medical device that looks similar to a trainer, with two adjustable pods underneath each shoe.</p><p>A trained clinician carefully positions these pods to change how forces travel through your joints as you walk. Your devices are fitted to you, with a programme shaped around your symptoms, movement and goals.</p></div></div><div class="featured-video reveal"><div class="featured-video-copy"><p class="eyebrow">See it for yourself</p><h3>Take a closer<br>look at Apos.</h3><p>Watch the video, then explore how treatment could fit into your everyday life.</p></div><div class="video-card" data-video-id="I_yi3L0aVDg" data-video-title="What is  Apos®"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: What is  Apos®"><img src={url('/assets/videos/I_yi3L0aVDg.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>An introduction to Apos®</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I_yi3L0aVDg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch What is  Apos® on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="how-it-works" class="apos-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>02 / How it works</span><span>Movement, thoughtfully adjusted</span></div><h2 class="reveal">Small adjustments.<br><span class="blue">A different way to move.</span></h2><div class="how-grid reveal"><article><span class="how-number">01</span><h3>Change how your<br>joints are loaded</h3><p>The position of the pods changes where pressure passes through your feet, helping shift load away from painful areas.</p></article><article><span class="how-number">02</span><h3>Help retrain<br>your movement</h3><p>The curved pods introduce small, controlled changes to your balance as you walk. These are designed to encourage adjustments in muscle control and walking patterns.</p></article><article><span class="how-number">03</span><h3>Build treatment<br>into your routine</h3><p>You’ll receive guidance on when and how long to wear your devices. Your wearing schedule is introduced gradually and reviewed as you progress.</p></article></div><div class="video-split reveal"><div class="video-card" data-video-id="4M-1dOPZQ4I" data-video-title="Effortless Success - How Apos® Works in the Background"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: Effortless Success - How Apos® Works in the Background"><img src={url('/assets/videos/4M-1dOPZQ4I.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Apos in everyday life</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4M-1dOPZQ4I" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch Effortless Success - How Apos® Works in the Background on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div><div class="video-editorial"><p class="eyebrow">Treatment in everyday life</p><h3>A programme that<br>fits into your day.</h3><p>Discover how Apos is designed to work alongside everyday activities. This video introduces the thinking behind the treatment and how wearing the devices becomes part of your routine.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section id="suitability" class="section suitability"><div class="suitability-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="mini-line"></span> Finding the right fit</p><h2>Could Apos be<br><span class="blue">right for you?</span></h2><a class="text-link" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Let’s discuss your options <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></div><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">Apos may be worth discussing if persistent knee, hip or lower-back pain is affecting how you walk or what you feel able to do.</p><p>An assessment helps establish whether the treatment is appropriate for your condition and whether you can use the devices safely. Your medical history, walking pattern and balance all matter.</p><div class="suitability-note"><h3>Your assessment matters.</h3><p>Apos is not suitable for everyone. Tell us about any unexplained falls, significant balance difficulties or walking aids you use, so we can advise you appropriately.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="treatment" class="treatment-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>03 / Your treatment journey</span><span>One step at a time</span></div><div class="treatment-layout"><div class="reveal"><h2>A clear plan,<br><span class="blue">with support<br>along the way.</span></h2></div><div class="journey reveal"><details open><summary><span>01</span>Start with a conversation<i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>Tell us what’s troubling you, what you’ve already tried and what you would like to feel able to do again. A free discovery call gives you space to ask questions before arranging an assessment.</p></details><details><summary><span>02</span>Understand your movement<i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>We’ll discuss your symptoms and assess how you walk. This helps us understand your starting point and explain the treatment options.</p></details><details><summary><span>03</span>Find your individual fit<i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>If Apos is suitable, your devices will be adjusted to your needs. You’ll receive clear instructions for using them and incorporating treatment into your routine.</p></details><details><summary><span>04</span>Review and adapt<i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>Follow-up appointments give us time to discuss changes, review your walking and adjust your devices and programme where needed.</p></details></div></div><div class="video-split assessment-video reveal"><div class="video-editorial"><p class="eyebrow">Your initial assessment</p><h3>Your first step,<br>explained.</h3><p>Knowing what to expect can make getting started feel easier. Take a closer look at an Apos initial assessment before arranging your own appointment.</p></div><div class="video-card" data-video-id="E1H_n9PAJQA" data-video-title="The Initial Assessment with Apos®"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: The Initial Assessment with Apos®"><img src={url('/assets/videos/E1H_n9PAJQA.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Your initial assessment</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E1H_n9PAJQA" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch The Initial Assessment with Apos® on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="evidence" class="section evidence-section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>04 / Clinical evidence</span><span>Informed choices</span></div><div class="intro-grid"><div class="reveal"><h2>An approach<br><span class="blue">supported<br>by research.</span></h2><a class="text-link evidence-link" href="https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/htg671" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the NICE guidance <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></div><div class="copy reveal"><p class="large-copy">Apos has been studied for knee osteoarthritis.</p><p>NICE recommends it as an option for certain adults whose non-surgical care has not worked well enough, who meet the referral criteria for knee replacement but do not want surgery, with long-term outcome data collected.</p><p>That recommendation applies to a defined group of patients. We’ll discuss how the evidence relates to your circumstances and what you can reasonably expect from treatment.</p></div></div><div class="expert-panel reveal"><div class="video-card" data-video-id="Xgt03le7JgU" data-video-title="Professor Oliver Pearce discusses knee health issues"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: Professor Oliver Pearce discusses knee health issues"><img src={url('/assets/videos/Xgt03le7JgU.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Expert discussion · Talking Knees</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xgt03le7JgU" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch Professor Oliver Pearce discusses knee health issues on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div><div class="video-editorial"><p class="eyebrow">Understanding knee health</p><h3>A closer look<br>at knee health.</h3><p>Understanding your knee health can help you ask better questions about your care. Watch Professor Oliver Pearce discuss knee health issues, then bring your own questions to a conversation with us.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="stories" class="video-stories-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>05 / Patient stories</span><span>In their own words</span></div><div class="video-stories-grid"><article class="reveal"><h3>What can progress look like?</h3><p>Watch this before-and-after example of knee treatment with Apos. It offers a visual perspective on one treatment experience; your own progress will depend on your circumstances.</p><div class="video-card" data-video-id="yavNtSz2YJs" data-video-title="Before and After Knee Treatment - Apos®"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: Before and After Knee Treatment - Apos®"><img src={url('/assets/videos/yavNtSz2YJs.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Before and after treatment</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yavNtSz2YJs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch Before and After Knee Treatment - Apos® on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div></article><article class="reveal"><h3>Hear it from people who’ve been there.</h3><p>What is treatment like from a patient’s perspective? Hear people share their experiences of Apos for knee and lower-back pain, in their own words.</p><div class="video-card" data-video-id="TebL6rl7tHc" data-video-title="Knee and Lower Back Pain Treatment Testimonials - Apos®"><div class="video-frame"><button class="video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play video: Knee and Lower Back Pain Treatment Testimonials - Apos®"><img src={url('/assets/videos/TebL6rl7tHc.jpg')} alt="" width="480" height="360" loading="lazy"><span class="play-circle" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></span><span class="video-play-label">Watch the video</span></button></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Patient experiences of Apos</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TebL6rl7tHc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Watch Knee and Lower Back Pain Treatment Testimonials - Apos® on YouTube, opens in a new tab">Watch on YouTube <svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></a></div></div></article></div></div></section>
<section id="written-stories" class="stories-section"><div class="section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>05 / Patient stories</span><span>Everyday life, rediscovered</span></div><div class="stories-heading reveal"><h2>What getting back to<br><span class="blue">everyday life can mean.</span></h2><div class="story-controls"><button class="circle-button" id="story-prev" aria-label="Previous testimonial"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 12H4M11 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg></button><span id="story-count" aria-live="polite">01 / 04</span><button class="circle-button" id="story-next" aria-label="Next testimonial"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></button></div></div><p class="stories-intro reveal">Hear from people who have shared their experience of treatment with Miles Physio.</p><div class="stories-track" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Patient testimonials. Use the arrow buttons or swipe to explore.">
<article class="story-card"><span class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span><blockquote>This is one of those examples of things that you have to try to believe. Both my father and I have used these. I had a huge knee trauma at 16. My knee was getting worse and worse. I'd had 5 operations on it. The surgeon said I had 10 years left with the knee when I was 38. Dad saw Apostherapy and we went. It took time but things got better and better. After 7 months I was playing squash again. After 12 months I went skiing. I had done either of those things since my 20's. It is wierd looking but it works. It's genius.</blockquote><div class="patient"><span class="patient-initials" aria-hidden="true">MB</span><div><strong>Matt Bradney</strong><span>Atrium Fitness Owner</span></div></div></article>
<article class="story-card"><span class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span><blockquote>Having played a lot of hockey for many years I was in a lot of pain with both my knees. Couple this with an occupation that involved a large amount of kneeling and my knees were very swollen and painful. Having worn the boots for over a year now, I feel completely different. I have much less pain and no swelling. I have even just started Couch to 5k.</blockquote><div class="patient"><span class="patient-initials" aria-hidden="true">SF</span><div><strong>Sue Field</strong><span>Retired Teacher</span></div></div></article>
<article class="story-card"><span class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span><blockquote>This note could not be big enough for the thanks I have for my AposTherapy boots and the people I have seen, in the last 3 years, checking my pain levels, stiffness, adjusting my boots and advice on how to help me live a pain-free knee and hip life. Now I do, I am back walking, aqua classes and enjoying everyday things that make life worthwhile again, Thank you, thank you, thank you, love Patricia Young xx</blockquote><div class="patient"><span class="patient-initials" aria-hidden="true">PY</span><div><strong>Patricia Young</strong><span>Essex patient</span></div></div></article>
<article class="story-card"><span class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span><blockquote>Treatment really does help relieve my knee joint problem. I am coming to the end of my 3 year programme and am still more mobile now than when the treatment commenced.</blockquote><div class="patient"><span class="patient-initials" aria-hidden="true">KC</span><div><strong>Keith Cambridge</strong><span>Essex patient</span></div></div></article>
</div><div class="story-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div></section>
<section id="pricing" class="section pricing-section"><div class="section-label reveal"><span>06 / Treatment pricing</span><span>Clear from the start</span></div><h2 class="reveal">Understand the cost<br><span class="blue">before you decide.</span></h2><div class="pricing-grid reveal"><article class="price-card starter"><span class="price-kicker">Getting started</span><h3>Apos starter package</h3><p class="price">£1,050</p><ul><li>Clinical assessment and walking analysis</li><li>One pair of individually adjusted Apos devices</li><li>Device fitting and personalised programme</li></ul><p class="assessment-note">If you are unsuitable or decide not to begin treatment, only the £100 assessment fee applies.</p><a class="button white-button" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Discuss treatment <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></article><article class="price-card"><span class="price-kicker">Ongoing support</span><h3>12-month maintenance</h3><p class="price">£400</p><ul><li>Three follow-up consultations</li><li>Walking analysis and progress review</li><li>Device adjustments and parts</li><li>Review of exercises and symptom management</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="mailto:info@milesphysio.com">Discuss maintenance <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></article><article class="price-card"><span class="price-kicker">As you need it</span><h3>Individual follow-up</h3><p class="price">£150</p><ul><li>One follow-up consultation</li><li>Review of symptoms and walking</li><li>Device adjustments</li><li>Review of your home programme</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="mailto:info@milesphysio.com">Arrange a follow-up <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a></article></div></section>
<section id="questions" class="faq-section"><div class="section faq-layout"><div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="mini-line"></span> Common questions</p><h2>A few things<br>you may be<br><span class="blue">wondering.</span></h2></div><div class="faq-list reveal"><details><summary>Where can I receive treatment?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Appointments are available in Chelmsford at Beaulieu Community Centre, online, or through a combination of both, depending on your needs. Clinic visits are by appointment.</p><p>Beaulieu Community Centre<br>Beaulieu Square, Centenary Way<br>Chelmsford, CM1 6AU</p></div></details><details><summary>Will my insurance cover treatment?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Some insurers cover Apos. Check your policy and obtain authorisation before treatment; we can help with questions about the process.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long will it take to notice a difference?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Progress varies. We’ll discuss realistic expectations at your assessment and review changes over time. Improvements are not guaranteed.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can Apos replace the need for surgery?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Apos is not a guaranteed alternative to surgery. Any decision to delay or proceed with joint replacement belongs in a discussion with your orthopaedic team.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do I need to decide before getting in touch?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>No. The discovery call is a chance to understand the treatment and ask questions before choosing your next step.</p></div></details></div></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="contact-section"><div class="contact-inner reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Let’s find<br>your <span>next step.</span></h2><div class="contact-copy"><p>You may have questions about the footwear, the programme or whether Apos could help with your symptoms.</p><p>Start with a conversation. We’ll listen to what matters to you and help you understand your options.</p><a class="button white-button" href="https://miles-physio.uk1.cliniko.com/bookings#service">Book your free discovery call <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12"/></svg></span></a><p class="contact-direct">Prefer to contact us directly?<br><a href="tel:+447980700940">07980 700 940</a><br><a href="mailto:info@milesphysio.com">info@milesphysio.com</a></p></div></div><div class="contact-ring" aria-hidden="true"></div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
